PS4 kernel: Baikal southbridge support (later CUH-21xx/22xx Slims and
CUH-71xx/72xx Pros). Without it the apcie driver fails on Baikal, so the GPU,
USB and SATA drivers wait for it forever and the TV gets no signal.

- ps4-apcie: on Baikal, no Aeolia MSI router; each function gets its own MSI,
  with the glue interrupt acknowledge (BAR2 0x110084/0x110088) run first.
  Register map from the ps4-linux 5.4 Baikal branch.
- ps4-apcie-icc: ICC registers in BAR2 on Baikal, polled instead of using
  its interrupt; USB ports powered on through the EMC as the 5.4 driver does.
- ahci/libahci and xhci-aeolia: the AHCI inside the Baikal XHCI function,
  with 1 ms polling because its interrupts stop after a few seconds. The
  polling approach and helpers are from rmuxnet's Baikal kernel
  (https://gitlab.com/rmuxnet/linux, GPL-2.0).

Only active when a Baikal southbridge is found; Aeolia and Belize are unchanged.
